    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-05192c98ec7f\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"no-else-if-discriminant-ts\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\belse\\\\s+if\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*[\\\\w$.]+\\\\.(kind|type|tag|_tag|variant)\\\\s*===?\\\\s*[\\\"'`]\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.ts\"},{\"id\":\"no-else-if-discriminant-tsx\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\belse\\\\s+if\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*[\\\\w$.]+\\\\.(kind|type|tag|_tag|variant)\\\\s*===?\\\\s*[\\\"'`]\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.tsx\"}],\"coverage\":\"Flags added lines in .ts and .tsx files that contain an `else if` comparing a conventional discriminant property (`.kind`, `.type`, `.tag`, `._tag`, `.variant`) to a string literal. This is the flagrant if/else-if dispatch over a union's variants.\",\"residual\":\"Does the edit branch over a closed set of mutually-exclusive variants in some way other than an exhaustive `switch` whose default calls `assertNever`? This covers else-if chains on other properties, enum members or reversed comparisons, and a switch with no assertNever default.\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/shape.ts b/src/domain/shape.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/shape.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\\n+export function area(s: { kind: \\\"circle\\\" } | { kind: \\\"square\\\" }): number {\\n+  if (s.kind === \\\"circle\\\") {\\n+    return 1;\\n+  } else if (s.kind === \\\"square\\\") {\\n+    return 2;\\n+  }\\n+  return 0;\\n+}\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/ui/badge.tsx b/src/ui/badge.tsx\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/ui/badge.tsx\\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\\n+export function label(e: { type: \\\"paid\\\" } | { type: \\\"due\\\" }): string {\\n+  if (e.type === \\\"paid\\\") {\\n+    return \\\"Paid\\\";\\n+  } else if (e.type === \\\"due\\\") {\\n+    return \\\"Due\\\";\\n+  }\\n+  return \\\"\\\";\\n+}\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/shape.ts b/src/domain/shape.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/shape.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\\n+import { assertNever } from \\\"./assert-never\\\";\\n+export function area(s: { kind: \\\"circle\\\" } | { kind: \\\"square\\\" }): number {\\n+  switch (s.kind) {\\n+    case \\\"circle\\\":\\n+      return 1;\\n+    case \\\"square\\\":\\n+      return 2;\\n+    default:\\n+      return assertNever(s);\\n+  }\\n+}\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"An else-if that compares a discriminant property to a string literal is a line-level, literal form of the forbidden chain, so it can be checked mechanically. Other things need semantics or multi-line structure: whether a set is closed, whether branches are mutually exclusive, other discriminants, and whether a switch is exhaustive with assertNever. These are left to the residual question.\"}",
